// Futura Round is NOT bundled or self-hosted, and must not be served to users.
//
// DECISION (FED lead, 2026-08-14): no Futura binaries in this repo. This is a licence
// constraint, not a preference. The EULA has been sighted — evidence, so this isn't
// re-litigated:
//
//   - The licence supplied with the font files is a Monotype "Font Software For Desktop
//     End User License Agreement", and it is the only one ("1 separate licenses are
//     listed below"). Located in the Zimmermann-Handover repo at
//     02-design/library/assets/Font Futura WOFF2/Licenses/2275/ (same file under the
//     OTF folder). Its "You may not" section prohibits, verbatim:
//         "Rent, lease, sublicense, give, lend, or further distribute the Font
//          Software, or any copy thereof"
//         "Install the Font Software on any server or in any digital asset management
//          system."
//     Its grant covers distributing materials only "provided that (a) the materials do
//     not contain the Font Software embedded". Committing .woff2 here and publishing
//     them to the Managed Runtime CDN does every prohibited thing at once.
//   - Provenance verified 2026-08-14: the 10 .woff2 previously in
//     overrides/app/static/fonts/ were byte-identical to the handover download, so they
//     carried exactly this licence.
//   - The F2R design workspace enforces the same rule — f2r/.gitignore excludes the
//     Futura OTF/WOFF2 folders, and no font binary exists anywhere on that branch.
//
// Reinstating self-hosted fonts requires Zimmermann's own Monotype Web Page Content
// entitlement AND a fresh download from Zimmermann's account. These handover files
// cannot become web-licensed by being passed along: the Desktop EULA's transfer clause
// requires the transferor to destroy all copies and permits "no change to the intent or
// scope of the rights granted". Scope needed is small — 2 Production Fonts (Regular 400,
// Medium 500); Monotype counts OTF and WOFF of one font as one.
//
// Type therefore renders from the fallback stack below. 'Futura Round' stays first so
// machines with the font installed locally still use it — which means designers and
// developers holding the desktop licence WILL see Futura Round while customers will
// NOT. Never sign off brand type from local rendering.
//
// Fallbacks mirror the prototype's font stack so Century Gothic / Gill Sans renders
// where available — much closer to the brand look than Arial.
// (Upstream token source: Handover tokens/typography.css.)
export const FONT_REGULAR =
  "'Futura Round', 'Futura LT Pro', 'Futura', 'Century Gothic', 'Gill Sans', 'Trebuchet MS', Arial, sans-serif";
export const FONT_MEDIUM =
  "'Futura Round', 'Futura LT Pro', 'Futura', 'Century Gothic', 'Gill Sans', 'Trebuchet MS', Arial, sans-serif";

// Source Serif 4 (400 italic) is the Handover's decorative serif accent, but no
// @font-face or .woff2 ships for it yet — this stack renders Georgia today.
// Self-host it (SIL OFL, free via Google Fonts) when a component first needs it.
export const FONT_SERIF = "'Source Serif 4', 'Georgia', serif";

export const fonts = {
  heading: FONT_MEDIUM,
  body: FONT_REGULAR,
  mono: FONT_REGULAR,
};

